{"id":"05a71f20509bfcd0","group":"58","path":"58/batch04/58-df-knot-invariant.md","title":"Knot Invariant","display":"df-knot-invariant — Knot Invariant","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-knot-invariant","aliases":["58-df-knot-invariant","Knot Invariant"],"display":"df-knot-invariant — Knot Invariant","depends_on":["[[../batch05/58-df-knot.md]]","[[../batch03/58-df-equivalence.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-knot-invariant"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-knot-invariant</span><span>Knot Invariant</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-knot-invariant — Knot Invariant"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ccaaf599ec318a33\" href=\"?note=ccaaf599ec318a33\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-knot.md\">../batch05/58-df-knot.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"1a891abf5fe2909c\" href=\"?note=1a891abf5fe2909c\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-equivalence.md\">../batch03/58-df-equivalence.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal K,Y,I,R\\in V\">\\(\\mathcal K,Y,I,R\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Knot}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{Knot}_S\\)</span> (knot predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"ccaaf599ec318a33\" href=\"?note=ccaaf599ec318a33\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-knot.md\">../batch05/58-df-knot.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EquivRel}\">\\(\\mathrm{EquivRel}\\)</span> (equivalence-relation predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"1a891abf5fe2909c\" href=\"?note=1a891abf5fe2909c\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-equivalence.md\">../batch03/58-df-equivalence.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> (set-function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{KnotInvariantStructure}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{KnotInvariantStructure}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{KnotInvariant}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{KnotInvariant}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (explicit predicate and compatibility projection defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}knot\\text{-}invariant\\text{-}explicit} \\vdash \\mathrm{KnotInvariantStructure}_S(I,\\mathcal K,Y,R)\\leftrightarrow\\mathcal K,Y\\in V\\land\\forall K\\in\\mathcal K\\;\\operatorname{Knot}_S(K)\\land\\mathrm{EquivRel}(R,\\mathcal K)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(I,\\mathcal K,Y)\\land\\forall K,K&#39;\\in\\mathcal K\\;(\\langle K,K&#39;\\rangle\\in R\\to I(K)=I(K&#39;))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}knot\\text{-}invariant\\text{-}explicit} \\vdash \\mathrm{KnotInvariantStructure}_S(I,\\mathcal K,Y,R)\\leftrightarrow\\mathcal K,Y\\in V\\land\\forall K\\in\\mathcal K\\;\\operatorname{Knot}_S(K)\\land\\mathrm{EquivRel}(R,\\mathcal K)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(I,\\mathcal K,Y)\\land\\forall K,K&#39;\\in\\mathcal K\\;(\\langle K,K&#39;\\rangle\\in R\\to I(K)=I(K&#39;))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}knot\\text{-}invariant\\text{-}projection} \\vdash \\mathrm{KnotInvariant}_S(I,Y)\\leftrightarrow\\exists\\mathcal K,R\\in V\\;\\mathrm{KnotInvariantStructure}_S(I,\\mathcal K,Y,R)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}knot\\text{-}invariant\\text{-}projection} \\vdash \\mathrm{KnotInvariant}_S(I,Y)\\leftrightarrow\\exists\\mathcal K,R\\in V\\;\\mathrm{KnotInvariantStructure}_S(I,\\mathcal K,Y,R)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The equivalence relation and knot domain are explicit in the structure predicate. The former formula used an unbound <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal K\">\\(\\mathcal K\\)</span> and an ambient-isotopy predicate absent from both dependencies.</li>\n<li>Knot invariant: quantity preserved under a chosen knot-equivalence relation; ambient isotopy is the intended instance</li>\n<li>Alexander polynomial: first discovered; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Delta_K(t) = \\Delta_K(t^{-1})\">\\(\\Delta_K(t) = \\Delta_K(t^{-1})\\)</span>; normalized</li>\n<li>Jones polynomial: from Hecke algebra; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Delta_K(t) = V_K(t)\">\\(\\Delta_K(t) = V_K(t)\\)</span> for knot with writhe correction</li>\n<li>Finite type: Vassiliev; invariants from chord diagrams; classify all via Kontsevich</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Jones, Hecke algebras and representation of braid groups</li>\n<li>Bar-Natan, On the Vassiliev Knot Invariants</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch05/58-df-knot.m